<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tattooed Serpent</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1725</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tattooed Serpent (died 1725) was the war chief of the Natchez in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> and brother of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-sun">Great Sun</a>, their paramount ruler. He generally kept peace with the French colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a>, and his funeral in 1725, at which wives and retainers were put to death to accompany him, was described in detail by the French settler Le Page du Pratz.</p></div>
